label Greeting
if {Transaction_HasReactiveOpener}:
	Brahim: {Transaction_ReactiveOpener}

if {Transaction_Chapter} == 0.0:
	# Chapter 1 — "Chalk and Bronze" (can / frozen + minigame:talisman:1 | 0 choice tally, +1 if won)
	Brahim: You must be the new keeper behind Lola's counter. I am Brahim, from past the creek bridge.
	Brahim: I used to teach up at the University of the Cordilleras in Baguio. Moved home to apprentice under Tatay.
	- Big jump from Baguio lectures to herbs!
		Brahim: My fingers are still better with whiteboard markers and bluebooks than bronze brushes, honestly.
	- Tatay is Karimlan's albularyo, right?
		Brahim: Forty years on that porch. High time I learned his craft so his hands can rest.
	- Miss the Baguio fog yet?
		Brahim: Only the cool air and strong coffee! Though Karimlan's warm breeze grows on you fast.
	Brahim: Speaking of steady hands, want to pair up on a quick lab exercise?
	Brahim: This is the First Ward, a simple starter sigil for fresh bronze. Mind tracing it with me?
	[signal arg="minigame:talisman:1"]
	if {Transaction_MinigameWon}:
		[signal arg="flag:brahim_steady_start=true"]
		[signal arg="tally:+1"]
		Brahim: Top marks, shopkeeper! Clean charcoal pillar, steady crimson crossbar. Even Tatay would nod at that.
	else:
		Brahim: Haha, every first draft needs a little character! Still hums better than my first five attempts.
	Brahim: Salamat for the practice. Let me grab [color=#0f6e2f]{Transaction_ItemWants}[/color] for Tatay's kitchen too.

elif {Transaction_Chapter} == 1.0:
	# Chapter 2 — "Margin Notes in the Librito" (sachet -> allow_sub_cat:bottle | Inflection #1)
	Brahim: Caught myself doing something ridiculous on Tatay's porch.
	Brahim: I started writing neat margin notes and color-coded tabs inside his handwritten librito like a course syllabus.
	Brahim: Tatay took one look, laughed, and told me to stop grading his orasyon and go smell actual lagundi leaves.
	Brahim: Old professor habits die hard! Sell me [color=#0f6e2f]{Transaction_ItemWants}[/color] so I can keep reviewing my notes.
	- [Swap his coffee for cold water.]
		[signal arg="allow_sub_cat:bottle"]
		Brahim: Salamat! Just need a quick cup before I cross-reference the pulse chapters.
	- Old professor habits die hard, ha?
		Brahim: Guilty as charged. At least Tatay has a good sense of humor about my sticky notes.
	- Just toss the notebook aside.
		[signal arg="tally:-1"]
		Brahim: Harsh critique, shopkeeper! Even folk craft deserves careful study, you know.

elif {Transaction_Chapter} == 2.0:
	# Chapter 3 — "What the Pulse Costs" (can + minigame:talisman:4 | Inflection #2)
	Brahim: Strange visit on Tatay's porch earlier. An old acquaintance offered me five hundred pesos cash.
	Brahim: Wanted a private luck charm rushed ahead of the neighbors waiting in line. Called it a consultation fee.
	Brahim: Back at UC Baguio, guest lectures came with a stipend. Here, Tatay says fixed cash hollows out an albularyo's gift.
	- Trust Tatay's rule. Keep it sacred.
		[signal arg="tally:+1"]
		Brahim: That settles it. Healing is a vocation answered with voluntary alay, never a price tag.
	- Charge a fee for your expertise.
		[signal arg="tally:-1"]
		Brahim: Practical, sure. Still, something about putting a rate card on prayer feels wrong in my chest.
	- Tell him to wait his turn.
		Brahim: Fair enough! First come, first served, same rule as office hours.
	if {Flag_BrahimSteadyStart}:
		Brahim: Since your brushwork scored top marks last time, mind helping me trace Watcher's Eye for the creek bridge?
	else:
		Brahim: Before I head back, mind helping me trace Watcher's Eye? It keeps mischief off the creek bridge.
	[signal arg="minigame:talisman:4"]
	if {Transaction_MinigameWon}:
		Brahim: Look at those fine gold lashes! Crisp as a textbook diagram, with real warmth in it.
	else:
		Brahim: A little wobbly around the iris, haha! No harm done, I will touch up the edges at Tatay's table.
	Brahim: Salamat, friend. Let me pick up [color=#0f6e2f]{Transaction_ItemWants}[/color] for dinner too.

elif {Transaction_Chapter} == 3.0:
	# Chapter 4 — "Cold Draft by the Guardrail" (pack + Moral Talisman Choice | Inflection #3)
	Brahim: Neighbors reported sudden cold spots and melted candle wax near the highway waiting shed.
	Brahim: Tatay's knees are swollen, so I am handling this solo. Sounds like a restless kaperosa by the bend.
	if {Flag_RosalynSeen} or {Flag_DaniloSawRosalyn}:
		- Wait. That is Rosalyn, she is harmless!
			Brahim: You know her? She visits your counter? Hold on, that changes my entire plan!
		- Sounds cold out by that guardrail.
			Brahim: Freezing, according to the tricycle drivers. Still, I do not want to hurt anyone by mistake.
	Brahim: I have two bronze blanks ready. Either a warm guiding lantern, or a strict wind barrier to clear the road.
	- Craft a warm lantern to guide.
		[signal arg="flag:brahim_lantern_ward=true"]
		[signal arg="tally:+1"]
		Brahim: Suki's Lantern. Crimson frame, gold core, indigo tassel. Help me trace it steady, friend.
		[signal arg="minigame:talisman:7"]
		if {Transaction_MinigameWon}:
			[signal arg="tally:+1"]
			Brahim: Look at that gold core glow! Gentle enough to steady a shy soul without pushing her away.
		else:
			Brahim: A bit uneven on the tassel, yet the warmth still holds. She will feel welcome, not chased.
	- Seal the road so she leaves.
		[signal arg="flag:brahim_lantern_ward=false"]
		[signal arg="tally:-1"]
		Brahim: Wind Shield it is. Strict charcoal crest and indigo chevron to close off the guardrail.
		[signal arg="minigame:talisman:10"]
		if {Transaction_MinigameWon}:
			Brahim: Sharp, clean barrier. Nothing restless will linger by that shed for long.
		else:
			Brahim: Rough edges, still heavy enough to push the cold draft back from the road.
	Brahim: Salamat for the brushwork. Let me grab [color=#0f6e2f]{Transaction_ItemWants}[/color] before I walk over to the bend.

elif {Transaction_Chapter} == 4.0:
	# Chapter 5 — "Smoke and Still Water" (can | 0 tallies — Ten Payoff!)
	if {Flag_BrahimLanternWard} and {Flag_DaniloTracedTether}:
		Brahim: You will not believe what happened when I hung Suki's Lantern by the waiting shed!
		Brahim: That laid-back guy from your bench walked over, squinted past the mist, and pointed straight across the creek.
		Brahim: He traced her tether two towns out so I knew exactly where to aim Tatay's calming orasyon!
	elif {Flag_BrahimLanternWard}:
		Brahim: Suki's Lantern worked like magic by the guardrail. The cold mist warmed right up without hurting a soul.
		Brahim: Tatay squeezed my shoulder when I got back and did not correct a single line in my notes.
	else:
		Brahim: The barrier ward cleared the highway bend, sure. The air went dead quiet right away.
		Brahim: Still sits heavy in my chest, honestly. Feels like I solved a symptom and missed the person underneath.
	- You listened instead of forcing it.
		Brahim: Funny how the best lessons in Karimlan happen when I finally close my notebook.
	- Sounds like Tatay would be proud.
		Brahim: He even poured me fresh lagundi tea without lecturing me once. High praise!
	- Glad the highway bend is quiet.
		Brahim: Quiet and safe, that is what matters.
	Brahim: Let me grab [color=#0f6e2f]{Transaction_ItemWants}[/color] for Tatay's porch.

elif {Transaction_Chapter} == 5.0:
	# Chapter 6 — "Tatay's Brass Bell" (pack + minigame:talisman:20 Grand Agimat | Accumulated Tally Resolution)
	if {Flag_BrahimLanternWard} and {Transaction_Tally} >= 3.0:
		[signal arg="outcome:true_albularyo"]
		Brahim: Tatay handed me his worn brass bell earlier. Said his hands are ready to rest and mine are ready to carry it.
		Brahim: Before I ring it for the barangay, I want us to trace one masterwork ward for Lola's counter.
		Brahim: The Grand Agimat. All four ritual inks, steady as you go!
		[signal arg="minigame:talisman:20"]
		if {Transaction_MinigameWon}:
			Brahim: Masterwork! Even my old UC Baguio dean would give that a standing ovation!
		else:
			Brahim: A few bold strokes on the outer ring, and it still hums warm as a hearth!
		Brahim: When Reyna Mayari weighs Karimlan's ledger, this albularyo stands right beside your counter, friend.
	elif {Transaction_Tally} >= 1.0:
		[signal arg="outcome:steady_apprentice"]
		Brahim: Still apprenticing at Tatay's pace, and loving every step of it. No rush to graduate!
		Brahim: Brought a Grand Agimat blank so we can ward your threshold together. Ready, lab partner?
		[signal arg="minigame:talisman:20"]
		if {Transaction_MinigameWon}:
			Brahim: Crisp lines all the way through! Your counter is in good hands.
		else:
			Brahim: Good effort on a tricky sigil! Still plenty warm enough to guard Lola's wood.
		Brahim: Salamat for keeping this little shop open for all of us.
	else:
		[signal arg="outcome:textbook_herbalist"]
		Brahim: I have Tatay's herbal notes organized neatly now. Practical work, steady results.
		Brahim: Here is a threshold ward for your counter, if you want to help trace it.
		[signal arg="minigame:talisman:20"]
		if {Transaction_MinigameWon}:
			Brahim: Clean geometry. That should keep drafts off your shelves.
		else:
			Brahim: Close enough for a standard ward.
	Brahim: Let me pick up [color=#0f6e2f]{Transaction_ItemWants}[/color] for Tatay's table too.

[end_timeline]

label Talk
Brahim: No rush at all. Still waiting on [color=#0f6e2f]{Transaction_ItemWants}[/color].
- Out of stock right now, Brahim.
	Brahim: No problem at all! I will swing back once Mario drops off a fresh crate.
	[signal arg="refuse_service"]
- Grabbing it right now!
	Brahim: Take your time, shopkeeper.
[end_timeline]

label Partial
set {Variation} = range(1,4).pick_random()
if {Variation} == 1.0:
	Brahim: Got that one, salamat! Still need [color=#0f6e2f]{Transaction_ItemWants}[/color] whenever you are ready.
elif {Variation} == 2.0:
	Brahim: Appreciate it! Just missing [color=#0f6e2f]{Transaction_ItemWants}[/color] to finish Tatay's list.
else:
	Brahim: One down, salamat. Pass over [color=#0f6e2f]{Transaction_ItemWants}[/color] too when you can.
[end_timeline]

label SubstituteItem
[signal arg="flag:brahim_sub_rest=true"]
[signal arg="tally:+1"]
Brahim: Wait a second. I asked for coffee, and you handed me [color=#0f6e2f]{Transaction_SubstituteItemName}[/color]?
Brahim: Haha, am I getting assigned mandatory hydration by my own storekeeper?
Brahim: Point taken! I will put the notebook down and take a breather. Salamat, friend.
[signal arg="story_success"]
[end_timeline]

label Satisfy
if {Transaction_StoryGouged}:
	Brahim: Whoa, steep markup on that one! Paying anyway, though Tatay is going to tease me about my budgeting.
else:
	if {Global_TipActive} == 1.0:
		Brahim: Keep the extra coins, shopkeeper! Good service deserves a tip.
	else:
		Brahim: Just what Tatay's kitchen needed. Salamat, friend!
[signal arg="story_success"]
[end_timeline]

label WrongItem
Brahim: Close, though I think that is a different item! I was looking for [color=#0f6e2f]{Transaction_ItemWants}[/color].
[end_timeline]
